IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `lb74-nouns`
IMPORT `lb74-cross-references`

-- Row il-74. TESTS THAT PIN THE READINGS of the item: the dates the footers print, the period the pages print, the days the row computed (typed, and again by the questions of lb74-nouns.l4), the comparison under each counting convention, both limbs, and how each limb was read.
-- These pass: they say what was read from what. The assertions that the last period printed ends on or after the day of publication, or on or after the day the commencement counts to, are in lb74-tests-red.l4 and fail; the four assertions of section "The comparisons the red module states, negated" below say the same thing from the other side, so that both counting conventions are pinned here as typed values and not as narration.
-- The expected values are hand-written from the quotation lines in lb74-cross-references.l4, from the printed pages and from calendar arithmetic done with Python date arithmetic on 2026-11-11 (NOTES.md), not copied from the values there.

§ `Tests of the readings`

-- The issue dates are the dates the footers print. They are issue dates, never days of effect.
#ASSERT `Sefer HaChukim 2036`'s `the issue date its footer prints` EQUALS Date 28 11 2005
#ASSERT `Sefer HaChukim 2232`'s `the issue date its footer prints` EQUALS Date 3 3 2010
#ASSERT `Sefer HaChukim 2350`'s `the issue date its footer prints` EQUALS Date 1 4 2012
#ASSERT `Sefer HaChukim 2387`'s `the issue date its footer prints` EQUALS Date 15 11 2012
#ASSERT `Sefer HaChukim 2647`'s `the issue date its footer prints` EQUALS Date 3 7 2017

-- The printed pages deposited.
#ASSERT `Sefer HaChukim 2036`'s `the printed pages deposited` EQUALS LIST 24
#ASSERT `Sefer HaChukim 2232`'s `the printed pages deposited` EQUALS LIST 407
#ASSERT `Sefer HaChukim 2350`'s `the printed pages deposited` EQUALS LIST 303, 308, 309, 311
#ASSERT `Sefer HaChukim 2387`'s `the printed pages deposited` EQUALS LIST 34
#ASSERT `Sefer HaChukim 2647`'s `the printed pages deposited` EQUALS LIST 1011

-- The citing words: item 1, paragraph (e), of the Third Schedule, on printed page 309 of SH 2350; it names section 230B.
-- The consolidation's line for paragraph (e) and the page's line are quoted in lb74-cross-references.l4.
#ASSERT `the citing words of item I1`'s `the item` EQUALS "I1"
#ASSERT `the citing words of item I1`'s `the item of the Third Schedule` EQUALS "1"
#ASSERT `the citing words of item I1`'s `the lettered paragraph, with letters in Latin` EQUALS "(e)"
#ASSERT `the citing words of item I1`'s `the printed page of the citing words` EQUALS 309
#ASSERT `the citing words of item I1`'s `the instrument that prints the citing words`'s `the issue date its footer prints` EQUALS Date 1 4 2012
#ASSERT `the citing words of item I1`'s `the citing words` EQUALS "החלטה של ועדה לעררים לעניין מצב תפקודי לפי סעיף 230ב לחוק הביטוח הלאומי"
#ASSERT `the citing words of item I1`'s `the number of the cited section, with letters in Latin` EQUALS "230B"
#ASSERT `the citing words of item I1`'s `the cited law, as the opening words of the item print it` EQUALS "חוק הביטוח הלאומי [נוסח משולב], התשנ״ה–1995"

-- The first period printed (SH 2036 section 2): words only, no calendar date.
#ASSERT `the first period printed for section 230B`'s `the delay before the commencement day, in months from publication, as the words print it` EQUALS 10
#ASSERT `the first period printed for section 230B`'s `the length from the commencement day, in years, as the words print it` EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `the first period printed for section 230B`'s `the instrument`'s `the issue date its footer prints` EQUALS Date 28 11 2005

-- The last period printed (SH 2232 section 1): the start day and the number of months are printed.
#ASSERT `the period SH 2232 prints for section 230B`'s `the number of months, as the words print it` EQUALS 30
#ASSERT `the printed start day` `the period SH 2232 prints for section 230B` EQUALS Date 29 9 2009
#ASSERT `the period SH 2232 prints for section 230B`'s `the instrument`'s `the issue date its footer prints` EQUALS Date 3 3 2010
#ASSERT `the period SH 2232 prints for section 230B`'s `the section of the instrument that prints it` EQUALS "1"

-- COMPUTATION: 29.9.2009 plus 30 calendar months is 29.3.2012; the last day is 28.3.2012 if the start day is day 1 of the months and 29.3.2012 if they are counted from the day after.
-- Calendar arithmetic written by hand, independent of the questions in lb74-nouns.l4:
#ASSERT Date 29 (9 PLUS 30) 2009 EQUALS Date 29 3 2012
#ASSERT Date 28 (9 PLUS 30) 2009 EQUALS Date 28 3 2012
#ASSERT `the same day of the month, the printed number of months after the start day` `the period SH 2232 prints for section 230B` EQUALS Date 29 3 2012
#ASSERT `the last day of the period if the start day is day 1 of the months` `the period SH 2232 prints for section 230B` EQUALS Date 28 3 2012
#ASSERT `the last day of the period if the months are counted from the day after the start day` `the period SH 2232 prints for section 230B` EQUALS Date 29 3 2012
#ASSERT `the last day of the period under the convention` `the period SH 2232 prints for section 230B` `the start day is day 1 of the months` EQUALS Date 28 3 2012
#ASSERT `the last day of the period under the convention` `the period SH 2232 prints for section 230B` `the months are counted from the day after the start day` EQUALS Date 29 3 2012
-- The days typed as computed agree with the questions:
#ASSERT `the last day of the period if the start day is day 1 of the months, as the row computed it`'s `the day` EQUALS Date 28 3 2012
#ASSERT `the last day of the period if the months are counted from the day after the start day, as the row computed it`'s `the day` EQUALS Date 29 3 2012
#ASSERT `the last day of the period if the start day is day 1 of the months, as the row computed it`'s `the day` EQUALS `the last day of the period if the start day is day 1 of the months` `the period SH 2232 prints for section 230B`
#ASSERT `the last day of the period if the months are counted from the day after the start day, as the row computed it`'s `the day` EQUALS `the last day of the period if the months are counted from the day after the start day` `the period SH 2232 prints for section 230B`

-- COMPUTATION: SH 2350 section 18(a) prints "60 days from its publication" and no calendar date.
#ASSERT `the number of days after publication that section 18(a) of SH 2350 prints for the commencement` EQUALS 60
#ASSERT Date ((Day (Date 1 4 2012)) PLUS 60) EQUALS Date 31 5 2012
#ASSERT Date ((Day (Date 1 4 2012)) PLUS 59) EQUALS Date 30 5 2012
#ASSERT Date ((Day (Date 1 4 2012)) PLUS 61) EQUALS Date 1 6 2012
#ASSERT `the day 60 days after the day SH 2350 was published, as the row computed it`'s `the day` EQUALS Date 31 5 2012
#ASSERT `the earliest day the 60 days can reach, as the row computed it`'s `the day` EQUALS Date 30 5 2012
#ASSERT `the latest day the 60 days can reach, as the row computed it`'s `the day` EQUALS Date 1 6 2012
#ASSERT `the day 60 days after the day SH 2350 was published, as the row computed it`'s `the day` EQUALS Date ((Day (`Sefer HaChukim 2350`'s `the issue date its footer prints`)) PLUS (`the number of days after publication that section 18(a) of SH 2350 prints for the commencement`))

-- The distance from the last day of the period to the day SH 2350 was published: 4 days under the first convention, 3 under the second (hand arithmetic: 28.3 to 1.4 is 4 days, 29.3 to 1.4 is 3).
#ASSERT `the number of days from the last day of the period under the convention to the day` `the period SH 2232 prints for section 230B` `the start day is day 1 of the months` (`Sefer HaChukim 2350`'s `the issue date its footer prints`) EQUALS 4
#ASSERT `the number of days from the last day of the period under the convention to the day` `the period SH 2232 prints for section 230B` `the months are counted from the day after the start day` (`Sefer HaChukim 2350`'s `the issue date its footer prints`) EQUALS 3
-- The distance to the day 31.5.2012: 64 days and 63 days.
#ASSERT `the number of days from the last day of the period under the convention to the day` `the period SH 2232 prints for section 230B` `the start day is day 1 of the months` (`the day 60 days after the day SH 2350 was published, as the row computed it`'s `the day`) EQUALS 64
#ASSERT `the number of days from the last day of the period under the convention to the day` `the period SH 2232 prints for section 230B` `the months are counted from the day after the start day` (`the day 60 days after the day SH 2350 was published, as the row computed it`'s `the day`) EQUALS 63

-- The comparisons the red module states, negated: each is FALSE under each counting convention (R1: against the day of publication; R2: against the day the commencement counts to).
#ASSERT NOT (`the last day of the period under the convention is on or after the day` `the period SH 2232 prints for section 230B` `the start day is day 1 of the months` (`Sefer HaChukim 2350`'s `the issue date its footer prints`))
#ASSERT NOT (`the last day of the period under the convention is on or after the day` `the period SH 2232 prints for section 230B` `the months are counted from the day after the start day` (`Sefer HaChukim 2350`'s `the issue date its footer prints`))
#ASSERT NOT (`the last day of the period under the convention is on or after the day` `the period SH 2232 prints for section 230B` `the start day is day 1 of the months` (`the day 60 days after the day SH 2350 was published, as the row computed it`'s `the day`))
#ASSERT NOT (`the last day of the period under the convention is on or after the day` `the period SH 2232 prints for section 230B` `the months are counted from the day after the start day` (`the day 60 days after the day SH 2350 was published, as the row computed it`'s `the day`))
-- The same holds for the earliest and the latest day the 60 days can reach, under each convention: the day the commencement counts to is after the last day of the period under any counting of the 60 days.
#ASSERT NOT (`the last day of the period under the convention is on or after the day` `the period SH 2232 prints for section 230B` `the months are counted from the day after the start day` (`the earliest day the 60 days can reach, as the row computed it`'s `the day`))
#ASSERT NOT (`the last day of the period under the convention is on or after the day` `the period SH 2232 prints for section 230B` `the months are counted from the day after the start day` (`the latest day the 60 days can reach, as the row computed it`'s `the day`))

-- POSITIVE CONTROL for the comparison: a probe period, made up here and read from no page (3 months from 29.1.2012), ends on 29.4.2012 or 28.4.2012, which is on or after 1.4.2012 under each convention.
-- It shows that the comparison used by the red module can say yes.
`a probe period of 3 months from 29.1.2012, not read from any page` MEANS
    `A period printed in months` WITH
        `the instrument` IS `Sefer HaChukim 2232`
        `the section of the instrument that prints it` IS "probe"
        `the section of the 2005 law the instrument amends` IS "probe"
        `the day of the month the period starts, as the words print it` IS 29
        `the month the period starts, as the words print it` IS 1
        `the year the period starts, as the words print it` IS 2012
        `the number of months, as the words print it` IS 3

#ASSERT `the last day of the period under the convention is on or after the day` `a probe period of 3 months from 29.1.2012, not read from any page` `the start day is day 1 of the months` (Date 1 4 2012)
#ASSERT `the last day of the period under the convention is on or after the day` `a probe period of 3 months from 29.1.2012, not read from any page` `the months are counted from the day after the start day` (Date 1 4 2012)
#ASSERT `the last day of the period under the convention` `a probe period of 3 months from 29.1.2012, not read from any page` `the start day is day 1 of the months` EQUALS Date 28 4 2012
#ASSERT `the last day of the period under the convention` `a probe period of 3 months from 29.1.2012, not read from any page` `the months are counted from the day after the start day` EQUALS Date 29 4 2012

-- Limb (a): under each convention the last period printed ends before the day SH 2350 was published.
#ASSERT `the last period printed ends before the citing instrument was published under the convention` `item I1: item 1(e) of the Third Schedule names section 230B of the National Insurance Law` `the start day is day 1 of the months`
#ASSERT `the last period printed ends before the citing instrument was published under the convention` `item I1: item 1(e) of the Third Schedule names section 230B of the National Insurance Law` `the months are counted from the day after the start day`
#ASSERT `limb (a) holds` `item I1: item 1(e) of the Third Schedule names section 230B of the National Insurance Law`
#ASSERT `item I1: item 1(e) of the Third Schedule names section 230B of the National Insurance Law`'s `limb (a) was read` EQUALS `official page images`

-- Limb (b): the instruments read that print words of the Third Schedule, and the items they name.
#ASSERT count (`item I1: item 1(e) of the Third Schedule names section 230B of the National Insurance Law`'s `the instruments read that print words of the Third Schedule`) EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `SH 2350 as an instrument that prints words of the Third Schedule`'s `the items of the Third Schedule its words name` EQUALS LIST "1"
#ASSERT `SH 2387 as an instrument that prints words of the Third Schedule`'s `the items of the Third Schedule its words name` EQUALS LIST "8"
#ASSERT `SH 2647 as an instrument that prints words of the Third Schedule`'s `the items of the Third Schedule its words name` EQUALS LIST "8"
#ASSERT NOT (`the instrument is later than the citing instrument and names the item` `item I1: item 1(e) of the Third Schedule names section 230B of the National Insurance Law` `SH 2350 as an instrument that prints words of the Third Schedule`)
#ASSERT NOT (`the instrument is later than the citing instrument and names the item` `item I1: item 1(e) of the Third Schedule names section 230B of the National Insurance Law` `SH 2387 as an instrument that prints words of the Third Schedule`)
#ASSERT NOT (`the instrument is later than the citing instrument and names the item` `item I1: item 1(e) of the Third Schedule names section 230B of the National Insurance Law` `SH 2647 as an instrument that prints words of the Third Schedule`)
#ASSERT `limb (b) holds` `item I1: item 1(e) of the Third Schedule names section 230B of the National Insurance Law`
#ASSERT `item I1: item 1(e) of the Third Schedule names section 230B of the National Insurance Law`'s `limb (b) was read` EQUALS `official page images, with the absence of a later instrument resting on the consolidation's tag list (CONSOLIDATION-ONLY)`
#ASSERT `both limbs hold` `item I1: item 1(e) of the Third Schedule names section 230B of the National Insurance Law`

-- POSITIVE CONTROL for limb (b): the same later instrument, made to name item 1, is detected (a probe, read from no page).
`a probe: SH 2647 made to name item 1, not read from any page` MEANS
    `An instrument that prints words of the Third Schedule` WITH
        `the instrument` IS `Sefer HaChukim 2647`
        `what its words do to the Third Schedule` IS "probe"
        `the items of the Third Schedule its words name` IS LIST "1"

#ASSERT `the instrument is later than the citing instrument and names the item` `item I1: item 1(e) of the Third Schedule names section 230B of the National Insurance Law` `a probe: SH 2647 made to name item 1, not read from any page`
#ASSERT NOT (`no instrument in the list is later than the citing instrument and names the item` `item I1: item 1(e) of the Third Schedule names section 230B of the National Insurance Law` (LIST `a probe: SH 2647 made to name item 1, not read from any page`))
